# Astryx (Working with AI)

Ref: [Working with AI](https://astryx.atmeta.com/docs/working-with-ai)

## Before writing Astryx UI

If you cannot answer all three without guessing, run the CLI first — do not invent props or import paths:

1. What is the correct import path for `Button`?
2. How do you make a `Dialog` non-dismissible?
3. What prop does `Selector` use for its items?

## CLI invocation (required)

Never call `node_modules/@astryxdesign/cli/bin/*.mjs` directly. Use the npm script alias:

```bash
pnpm exec astryx <cmd>
# examples:
pnpm exec astryx component Dialog --dense
pnpm exec astryx docs tokens --dense
pnpm exec astryx build "settings page"
```

Use `--dense` when pasting CLI output into context. After `@astryxdesign/core` bumps, re-run `pnpm exec astryx init --features agents` and `pnpm exec astryx upgrade --apply`.

## MCP

This project configures the Astryx MCP server in `.cursor/mcp.json`. Prefer `search` / `get` over guessing when the server is available.

## Project note

All UI uses Astryx (`@astryxdesign/core`). Templates live under `src/react-app/ui/`. Follow `.cursor/rules/features-structure.mdc` for folder placement. Do not add Radix/shadcn components — use `pnpm exec astryx component <Name>` to discover APIs.

## Page titles: breadcrumbs only

The dashboard shell (`ShellSideNavLayout`) already renders the page title + description via `AppBreadcrumbs`. Pages inside the shell must NOT render their own page-level heading — no `<Heading level={1}>` / `LayoutHeader` duplicating the breadcrumb label.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — "Settings" appears twice (breadcrumb + page header)
<Layout header={<LayoutHeader><Heading level={1}>{lang.title}</Heading></LayoutHeader>} … />

// ✅ GOOD — no page header; breadcrumbs own the title
<Layout start={…} content={…} />
```

Section headings inside the page body (`Heading level={3}` in a settings panel, card titles) are fine — only the top-level page title is owned by breadcrumbs. When adding a new page, register its title/description in `resolveDashboardHeaderText` (`shared/i18n`) instead of rendering text in the page.

